$test['Pets'] = 'A black Labrador waits at the front door with a leash already in its mouth ears lifted and tail caught mid-wag. Soft Black and Grey Realism keeps the dog sharp while the door and floor fade quickly into skin'
$cats['Pets']['Pets II Everyday Rituals'] = @('A black Labrador waits at the front door with a leash already in its mouth ears lifted and tail caught mid-wag. Soft Black and Grey Realism keeps the dog sharp while the door and floor fade quickly into skin','A grey tabby sits inside an empty cardboard box that is clearly too small with its paws tucked and eyes half closed. Fine Line drawing with soft grey shading keeps the box simple and the cat full of personality','A Beagle sniffs along the ground with its nose low and ears dragging through fallen leaves. Illustrative linework follows the scent path as a faint winding line that leads off the edge of the design','A Siberian cat stretches across a sunny windowsill with one paw hanging over the edge. Warm Colour Realism light falls across the fur while the window frame is suggested with only two clean lines','A Corgi sits perfectly still beside a food bowl staring upward with total focus. Neo-Traditional color and bold outlines make the begging expression the whole story','A parakeet perches on the rim of a coffee mug leaning in to inspect the steam. Delicate Colour Realism keeps the green and yellow feathers vivid while the mug stays in simple grey','An old Shepherd mix lies with its chin resting on a pair of worn work boots by the door. Black and Grey Realism treats the boots and the grey muzzle with the same care','A Bengal cat bats at a dangling string toy caught mid-swipe with one paw raised. Sketch lines show the earlier paw positions while the spotted coat resolves in rich color','A horse lowers its head over a stable door to accept an apple from a hand. Fine Line drawing focuses on the soft muzzle whiskers and the open palm','A Pug sleeps on its back with all four paws in the air and its tongue slightly out. Clean Illustrative linework with soft shading makes the pose both funny and loving')
$cats['Pets']['Pets II One Detail Is Enough'] = @('Only the eye of a Husky is shown one icy blue iris with the fur around it fading out in fine lines. Colour Realism keeps the blue electric against black and grey fur','A single cat ear with a small notch from an old fight is rendered at large scale. Dotwork shading builds the inner fur and the scar while everything else is left out','The wet nose and whiskers of a Boxer fill the composition seen extremely close. Black and Grey Realism turns the nose texture into something almost sculptural','A horses mane is shown blowing sideways with only the edge of the eye and ear visible at the top. Loose ink-wash strokes make the hair feel like moving water','A dogs front paw rests on a human hand the two shapes overlapping. Fine Line drawing keeps both simple while the paw pads get soft grey shading','The curled tail of a Shiba Inu is drawn as one bold sweeping shape in rust orange and cream. The rest of the dog is suggested only by the line of its back','A rabbits two long ears stand upright one slightly bent rendered in soft Dotwork. The head below them disappears into skin','The patterned scales along the back of a pet corn snake are shown in a tight S curve. Orange red and cream Colour Realism keeps the real markings exact','A single feather from a pet cockatoo with its pale yellow tint floats at an angle. Fine Line edges and soft color keep it light and airy','The worn leather of a dog collar wraps around a small brass tag seen from above. Black and Grey Realism shows every scratch and stitch')
$cats['Pets']['Pets II Pets In Motion'] = @('A Jack Russell leaps straight up to catch a ball all four legs off the ground. Sketch movement lines trace the jump while the dog itself is crisp and full of energy','A Dalmatian runs along a beach with water splashing from its paws. Black spots and white fur stay graphic while the splash breaks into loose ink','A cat leaps between two shelves body fully stretched in mid-air. Illustrative linework shows the long reach of the front legs and the trailing tail','A Greyhound turns a tight corner at full speed body leaning sharply. Black and Grey shading shows the muscle while motion streaks follow the curve','A Golden Retriever shakes water off its coat droplets spraying outward in a ring. Colour Realism catches warm sunlight in each drop','A horse and rider jump a low fence shown from the side at the top of the arc. Fine Line drawing keeps the shape clean and light','A ferret dances sideways with its back arched the funny hop it does when excited. Illustrative lines with light brown shading capture the strange happy pose','A Border Collie crouches low eyes locked forward about to herd. Black and Grey Realism focuses on the intense stare and tense shoulders','A rabbit mid-binky twists in the air with its ears flying. Watercolour splashes of soft brown and lavender follow the twist','A parrot flaps its wings wide while perched on a shoulder feathers spread in full color. The person is just a simple line while the bird is detailed Colour Realism')
$cats['Pets']['Pets II Home and Place'] = @('A cat sits on the hood of a parked car in a driveway at dusk watching the street. The car and house are faint outlines while the cat is a dark detailed silhouette','A dogs bed by a fireplace holds a sleeping Bulldog curled tight. Warm Colour Realism firelight touches the wrinkles and fur','A horse stands in an open field at the fence line looking toward a farmhouse in the distance. Black and Grey shading gives depth while the sky fades to skin','A dogs head pokes out of a tent flap on a camping trip ears flopped and eyes bright. Illustrative linework keeps the tent simple and the face expressive','A cat sits inside a potted plant on a balcony surrounded by leaves. Fine Line plants with a few green accents frame the cats serious face','A Basset Hound lies flat on a porch with ears spread across the boards. Black and Grey Realism enjoys the long ears and droopy eyes','A fish tank glows in a dark room with a single betta fish trailing its long fins. Colour Realism makes the fins glow blue and red against black water','A dog stands in the bed of an old pickup truck ears blowing back. Neo-Traditional color and bold lines give it a classic road-trip feel','A cat watches rain from inside its reflection faint in the wet window glass. Black and Grey Realism shows both the cat and its ghostly reflection','A tortoise walks slowly across a garden path between flowers. Colour Realism shows the patterned shell while flowers stay in fine line')
$cats['Pets']['Pets II Pet and Person'] = @('A man sleeps on a couch with a large dog sprawled across his chest. Fine Line drawing keeps both figures simple and the moment intimate','A woman braids her horses mane both shown from behind. Black and Grey shading focuses on her hands and the twisted hair','A child-sized hand and a puppy paw rest side by side on a wooden floor. Simple Fine Line drawing with soft shading keeps it clean','A cat sits on a persons shoulder both looking the same direction out of a window. Illustrative linework makes their matching posture the joke and the bond','Two hands cup a hamster which peeks over the thumb. Colour Realism keeps the tiny face sharp and the hands soft','A man and his dog sit side by side on a dock seen from behind both looking at the water. The silhouettes are solid black against fine line water','A woman lies in tall grass while her dog lies beside her with its head on her stomach. Watercolour greens with fine line figures','A runner jogs at dawn with a dog on a leash beside her both in step. Sketch lines show motion while the two figures resolve in black','A man holds a horses lead rope while the horse rests its head over his shoulder. Black and Grey Realism focuses on the two faces close together','A grandmother knits while a cat sleeps on the ball of yarn in her lap. Fine Line drawing with a few soft color accents in the yarn')
$cats['Pets']['Pets II Small and Unusual Companions'] = @('A hedgehog curls half into a ball with its nose and tiny feet still showing. Dotwork builds every spine while the face stays soft','A chinchilla sits upright holding a piece of food its fur rendered as soft grey Dotwork. Big dark eyes stay sharply resolved','A pet tarantula rests on an open palm legs spread naturally. Black and Grey Realism shows the fuzzy texture without making it frightening','A pet duck waddles forward with a confident chest-out walk. Illustrative linework with soft yellow and white color','A crested gecko clings upside down to a branch looking straight at the viewer. Colour Realism shows the textured skin in rust and cream','A pet goat stands on top of a wooden spool proud of its climb. Neo-Traditional color and bold outlines','A pet pig lies in mud with a happy face ears flopped forward. Watercolour browns and pinks with clean linework on the face','A pet chicken stands with its feathers fluffed its comb bright red. Colour Realism with a soft background fade','An axolotl in a home tank smiles its natural smile pink gills spread. Delicate color with fine line bubbles','A pet crow perches on a wrist head tilted holding a small shiny button in its beak. Black and Grey Realism shows the glossy feathers')
$cats['Pets']['Pets II Light Season and Weather'] = @('A black dog stands in falling snow flakes collecting on its back and nose. Black and Grey Realism with white snow left as untouched skin','A cat sits in a patch of autumn leaves its orange fur matching the leaves around it. Colour Realism with warm reds and golds','A horse stands in morning fog only its head and front legs clear. Soft Black and Grey shading fades the rest into mist','A dog sits under a summer sprinkler soaked and delighted mouth open. Colour Realism catches rainbow light in the spray','A cat sleeps in a single beam of light from a skylight while the rest of the room is dark. High contrast Black and Grey shading','A rabbit sits among spring tulips ears up. Watercolour pinks and greens with fine line detail on the face','A dog walks through a puddle on a rainy street its reflection broken in the water. Black and Grey Realism with soft streetlight glow','A parrot sits in tropical sunset light its feathers glowing orange at the edges. Colour Realism with rich warm tones','A horses breath steams in cold winter air as it looks toward the viewer. Black and Grey Realism with soft white breath','A cat watches fireflies at night from a porch step. Dark Blackwork night with tiny yellow glowing dots')
$cats['Pets']['Pets II Saying Goodbye Differently'] = @('An empty dog bed with a single toy left in the middle seen from above. Fine Line drawing simple and quiet','A cats silhouette is formed by the shape of open sky between tree branches. Blackwork branches with the cat as untouched skin','A dog walks away down a country road toward a bright horizon tail up. Black and Grey shading with light at the end of the road','A horses halter hangs on an empty stable hook with morning light falling on it. Black and Grey Realism focuses on worn leather','A pair of footprints in sand walk beside a set of paw prints that slowly fade. Fine Line very minimal','A dogs portrait is formed from the leaves of a growing tree. Illustrative linework with soft green accents','A cat curls up inside the moons crescent asleep among faint stars. Fine Line with soft grey shading','A rabbit sits at the edge of a meadow watching a sunset seen from behind. Watercolour sunset with a small dark silhouette','A dogs water bowl reflects a sky full of clouds instead of the room. Black and Grey Realism with a surreal touch','A bird flies out of an open cage door into open sky the cage drawn in fine line and the bird in color')
$cats['Pets']['Pets II Art Styles Reimagined'] = @('A Bulldog is drawn as a classic American Traditional flash piece with bold outlines red collar and a banner left blank','A Siamese cat is rendered in Japanese woodblock style with flat color waves and a single maple leaf','A Labradors face is built from geometric triangles that dissolve into fur at the edges','A horse head is drawn in Art Nouveau style with flowing mane forming a decorative frame','A tabby cat appears in pop-art style with bold dots and bright flat colors','A German Shepherd is drawn as a woodcut print with heavy black carved lines','A parrot is rendered in stained-glass style with bright colored sections and black lead lines','A Pomeranian is drawn as a cute New School character with big eyes and fluffy exaggerated fur','A Doberman is drawn as a single continuous line never lifting the pen','A Persian cat is rendered in soft Chicano-style black and grey with ornate lettering space left blank below')
$cats['Pets']['Pets II Push Pets'] = @('A dog sits in the center of a vinyl record the grooves circling it like ripples. Black and Grey Realism with a warm brown label behind the dog','A cats body forms the shape of a crescent moon while it sleeps with stars caught in its fur. Fine Line with soft blue accents','A horse gallops out of an open book the pages turning into its mane. Black and Grey Realism with fine line pages','A dogs portrait is reflected in a pair of sunglasses worn by its owner only the lenses and nose bridge shown. Colour Realism reflection','A cat sits inside a snow globe on a shelf snow falling around it. Colour Realism glass with soft reflections','A rabbit is made of clouds drifting across a blue sky with only its eye and nose clearly drawn. Soft watercolour blues','A dog runs through a field that turns into a starry night sky behind it. Colour Realism foreground fading into deep blue Dotwork stars','A parrots tail feathers turn into a rainbow of paint brush strokes. Colour Realism head with loose painterly tail','A cat and dog sleep curled together to form a yin-yang shape one black and one white. Clean Blackwork','A horse made entirely of flowing water rears up with the shape of the horse held by light and splash. Colour Realism blues and whites')
$b['A black Labrador waits at the front door with a leash already in its mouth ears lifted and tail caught mid-wag. Soft Black and Grey Realism keeps the dog sharp while the door and floor fade quickly into skin'] = 'Two panels side by side on one image, divided down the middle. LEFT PANEL: the tattoo design alone on a plain white background, shown flat exactly as described, no body, drawn large so it fills most of the panel. RIGHT PANEL: Studio photograph of a real person''s body showing the same exact tattoo where described, healed tattoo on real skin in soft even light, the rest of the body modestly covered by simple plain clothing, only the tattooed area bare, plain seamless light grey studio backdrop - no room, no furniture, no scenery. The tattoo in both panels is identical. The tattoo: A black Labrador waits at the front door with a leash already in its mouth, ears lifted and tail caught mid-wag. Soft Black and Grey Realism keeps the dog sharp while the door and floor fade quickly into skin. Hopeful, loyal, familiar. In the right panel it is on a man, outer forearm. Create exceptional contemporary tattoo inspiration centered on a specific beloved pet. PETS = WHO I LOVE. The emotional subject is not a generic species. It is one individual animal. The example animal shown in each concept is only an example. NEVER LET THE EXAMPLE PET BECOME THE DESIGN. THE DESIGN MUST STILL WORK WHEN THE CUSTOMER REPLACES THE EXAMPLE WITH THEIR OWN PET. If the concept shows a Doberman, the underlying artistic idea should still work with a Golden Retriever, mixed-breed dog, cat, rabbit, horse, bird or another companion animal whenever logically appropriate. Rotate pets continuously. Do not create a catalog dominated by one or two popular breeds. Include a broad natural mix of dogs, cats, horses, rabbits, birds, reptiles, small mammals and unusual companion animals. Within dogs, rotate breeds, sizes, coat types, ages and appearances. Within cats, rotate coat patterns, breeds, body types and ages. Include mixed-breed animals. Include senior animals. Include young animals. Include rescued animals. Include animals with physical characteristics that make them individually recognizable. Do not beautify away identity. If the real dog has one ear that sits differently, preserve it. If the cat has a torn ear, preserve it. If the senior animal has a grey muzzle, preserve it. If the pet has one eye, preserve it. If the animal has an unusual tooth, scar, coat patch, blaze, feather pattern, scale pattern or posture, preserve it. INDIVIDUALITY IS MORE IMPORTANT THAN BREED PERFECTION. Use the full artistic vocabulary of tattooing. Realism. Black and Grey Realism. Colour Realism. Micro Realism. Fine Line. Sketch. Dotwork. Blackwork. Watercolour. Illustrative. Neo-Traditional. New School. Geometric. Negative Space. Ornamental. Surrealism. And intelligent combinations. Do not rotate styles mechanically. Choose a style because it improves the specific idea. A realistic portrait may be right when exact likeness is the emotional center. Sketch may be right when movement or memory is important. Watercolour may be right when softness or color carries the feeling. Blackwork may be right for a dark animal or powerful silhouette. Fine Line may be right for intimacy and restraint. Dotwork may be right for texture. New School may be right for a pet with enormous personality. Ornamental treatment may be right when the pet is being elevated into something precious. The style serves the relationship. Pet tattoos do not always need the pets face. Explore: Actual paw prints. Actual nose prints. Actual collars. Actual tags. Actual toys. Actual blankets. Actual feathers. Actual horseshoes. Favorite objects. Favorite sleeping positions. Favorite places. Favorite walks. Daily routines. Car rides. Windows. Beds. Chairs. Trails. Hands touching fur. Forehead-to-forehead contact. The way an animal looked back. The way it waited. The way it slept. The way it ran. The way it sat beside someone. The ordinary behavior may contain more emotional truth than a formal portrait. DO NOT USE GENERIC PAW PRINTS WHEN THE CONCEPT CALLS FOR THE CUSTOMERS ACTUAL PAW PRINT. DO NOT USE GENERIC TAGS WHEN THE CUSTOMERS REAL TAG CAN BE USED. DO NOT INVENT PERSONAL DETAILS. The design should invite personalization. Multiple pets must form one composition. Do not default to stacking floating animal heads. Show relationships. Pets can sleep together. Run together. Walk together. Touch noses. Share furniture. Occupy the same environment. Interact naturally. If portrait composition is used, connect the portraits through deliberate structure rather than merely arranging heads vertically. MEMORIAL IS PART OF PETS. MEMORIAL IS NOT ALL OF PETS. Living pets should be celebrated just as strongly. Joy does not require comedy. Show companionship. Energy. Trust. Age. Habit. Comfort. Adventure. Home. Personality. Affection. Memorial concepts should avoid automatic cliches. Do not automatically add: Angel wings. Halos. Heavenly clouds. Generic infinity symbols. Generic heartbeat lines. Generic paw icons. RIP text. Clocks. Dates surrounded by decorative filler. These elements can be used when specifically meaningful to the customer, but death itself does not require a visual symbol. Sometimes the empty collar is enough. Sometimes the sleeping position is enough. Sometimes the old tennis ball is enough. Sometimes the grey muzzle is enough. Sometimes the familiar window is enough. Sometimes the animal simply walking away is enough. Design for the body. Do not place a rectangular photograph on skin. Allow portraits to fade naturally. Allow full bodies to follow anatomy. Allow horses to use long placements. Allow birds to open across shoulders. Allow snakes and long-bodied pets to wrap. Allow sleeping animals to form natural curved compositions. Allow multiple pets enough space to interact. Use small tattoos where intimacy benefits from small scale. Use medium tattoos for most portrait and relationship concepts. Use large scale only when the artistic idea deserves it. Do not make everything a portrait. Do not make everything memorial. Do not make everything sentimental. Do not make everything cute. Do not make everything realistic. Do not make everything Fine Line. Do not make everything a dog. Do not make everything a cat. Do not make everything a Golden Retriever. Do not make everything a Maine Coon. Do not make every animal young and perfect. Do not use generic breed stereotypes as personality. The customers animal provides the personality. THE PET IS NOT A SYMBOL UNTIL THE CUSTOMER MAKES IT ONE. THE PET IS FIRST A RELATIONSHIP. The goal of every inspiration image is for someone to think: THAT IS NOT MY PET. BUT I WANT THAT IDEA WITH MY PET'
